{"version":1,"slug":"Others__Quantitative_Aptitude_-_SSC_Super_Practice_41648_(20Q)","path":"Others/Quantitative Aptitude - SSC Super Practice 41648 (20Q).html","title":"devgagan","provider":"Others","category":"Quantitative Aptitude - SSC Super Practice 41648 (20Q).html","durationMinutes":60,"totalQuestions":20,"sectionsLocked":false,"sections":null,"questions":[{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Find the sum of <img width=81 height=27 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p5108/image005.png\"> and &radic;(1215 + 9<sup>2</sup>).</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p><img width=\"81\" height=\"27\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p5108/image005.png\"> &#2324;&#2352; &radic;(1215 + 9<sup>2</sup>) &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">43</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">43</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">47</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">47</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">55</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">55</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">65</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">65</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Let a = <img width=81 height=27 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p5108/image005.png\"> and b = &radic;(1215 + 9<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>a = <img width=81 height=27 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p5108/image005.png\"></p><p>a = &radic;(832 + 9)</p><p>a = &radic;(841)</p><p>a = 29</p><p>b = &radic;(1215 + 9<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>b = &radic;(1215 + 81)</p><p>b = &radic;(1296)</p><p>b = 36</p><p>a + b = 29 + 36 = 65</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which of the following statement is true?</p><p>I. 29<sup>56</sup>+67<sup>87</sup> is a prime number.</p><p>II. 146<sup>61</sup> - 88<sup>41</sup> is a prime number.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2366; &#2325;&#2341;&#2344; &#2360;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p>I. 29<sup>56</sup>+67<sup>87</sup> &#2319;&#2325; &#2309;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;|</p><p>II. 146<sup>61</sup> - 88<sup>41</sup> &#2319;&#2325; &#2309;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;|</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Only II</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; II</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Only I</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; I</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Both I and II</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">I &#2324;&#2352; II &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Neither I nor II</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2344; &#2340;&#2379; I &#2324;&#2352; &#2344; &#2361;&#2368; II</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>I. When an odd number is multiplied by itself multiple times, then solution gives an odd value. So, 29<sup>56</sup> and 67<sup>87</sup> are odd.</p><p>Addition of two odd number always gives an even value. So, 29<sup>56</sup>+67<sup>87</sup> is even and an even number cannot be a prime number.(except 2, which is not possible in this case)</p><p>Hence, statement I is wrong.</p><p>II. When an even number is multiplied by itself multiple times, then solution gives an even value. So, 146<sup>61</sup> and 88<sup>41</sup> are even.(except 2, which is not possible in this case)</p><p>Addition of two even number always gives an even value. So, 146<sup>61</sup> - 88<sup>41</sup> is even and an even number cannot be a prime number.</p><p>Hence, statement II is wrong.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which of the following is not a prime number?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2309;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">17</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">17</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">29</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">29</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">69</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">69</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">97</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">97</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Since 69 is divisible by 3, hence it is not a prime number.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>What is the square root of [2896  -  (45 x 60)]? </p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>[2896 - (45 x 60)] &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327;&#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">10</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">12</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">12</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">14</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">14</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">16</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">16</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Square root of [2896  -  (45 x 60)]</p><p>= square root of [2896  -  2700]</p><p>= square root of 196</p><p>= <b>14</b></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If one number is 13/15 times of another number and difference between the two numbers is 12, then what is sum of both numbers?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; 13/15 &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; 12 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">134</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">134</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">128</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">128</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">168</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">168</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">132</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">132</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Let one number is a and another number be b.</p><p>a/b= 13/15</p><p>Let a = 13k and b = 15k</p><p>So, b - a = 12</p><p>=&gt; 15k  -  13k = 12</p><p>=&gt; k = 6</p><p>Hence, sum of both numbers = 13 * 6 + 15 * 6 = 168</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>How can Two-Third of 15% be written in decimal form?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>15% &#2325;&#2366; &#2342;&#2379;-&#2340;&#2368;&#2361;&#2366;&#2312; &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">0.1</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">0.1</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">0.01</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">0.01</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1.0</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1.0</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">10</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>According to Question,</p><p>Two-Third of 15%= 2/3<sup>rd</sup> of 15%</p><p>=2/3 x 15/100</p><p>=10/100</p><p>=1/10</p><p>=0.1 Ans.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Find the square of number of odd numbers between 5 and 33.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>5 &#2324;&#2352; 33 &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2367;&#2359;&#2350; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">121</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">121</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">225</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">225</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">169</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">169</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">196</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">196</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>According to Question,</p><p>Single digits odd number between 5 and 33 are 2</p><p>And, double digit odd numbers between 5 and 33 are 11</p><p>Total odd Numbers = 2+11=13</p><p>Square of the number of digits = 13 *13 = 169 Ans.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If x is an odd number and y is an even number, then which of the following is an odd number?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; x &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2359;&#2350; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; y &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2359;&#2350; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">x + y + 1</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">x + y + 1</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">xy</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">xy</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">xy + y</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">xy + y</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">x + y + 2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">x + y + 2</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>x = odd, so let x = 2n + 1, where n is any positive integer</p><p>y = even, so let y = 2m, where m is any positive integer</p><p>x + y + 1 = 2n + 1 + 2m + 1 = 2n + 2m + 2 = 2(n + m + 1), which is even</p><p>xy = (2n + 1)2m = 2m(2n + 1), which is even</p><p>xy + y = 2m(2n + 1) + 2m = 2m(2n + 2), which is even</p><p>x + y + 2 = 2n + 1 + 2m + 2 = 2n + 2m + 3 = 2(n + m + 1) + 1, so it is odd.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which is the largest fraction among 4/13, 7/11, 8/15 and 4/9?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>4/13, 7/11, 8/15 &#2324;&#2352; 4/9 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">7/11</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">7/11</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4/13</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4/13</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">8/15</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">8/15</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4/9</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4/9</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>4/13, 7/11, 8/15 and 4/9</p><p>= 1980/6435, 4095/6435, 3432/6435, and 2860/6435</p><p>Largest = 4095/6435 = 7/11</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Express the decimal number 9.825 in fraction.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 9.825 &#2325;&#2379; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">89/25</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">89/25</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">393/40</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">393/40</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">72/23</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">72/23</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">43/7</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">43/7</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>To express 9.825 in fraction, we have to remove the decimal</p><p>So, 9.825 = 9825/1000</p><p>Deducing it to lowest fraction, we get;</p><p>9.825 = 393/40 Ans.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>How many prime numbers are there from 200 to 267?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>200 &#2360;&#2375; 267 &#2340;&#2325; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2309;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">10</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">11</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">11</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">12</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">12</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">9</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">9</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>All prime numbers between 200 and 267 = (211, 223, 227, 229, 233, 239, 241, 251, 257, 263)</p><p>Total 10 prime numbers are there between 200 and 267.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which of the following is smaller than 1/5?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2368; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; 1/5 &#2360;&#2375; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">2/7</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2/7</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1/4</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1/4</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1/6</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1/6</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1/3</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1/3</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>1/5 = 0.2</p><p>2/7 = 0.28, 1/4 = 0.25, 1/6 = 0.166, 1/3= 0.333</p><p>So, 1/6 &lt; 1/5</p><p>Also, if a fraction has numerator = 1 and denominator &gt; 5, it will be smaller than 1/5.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>What is the value of &radic;8&radic;1.28?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&radic;8&radic;1.28 &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">0.32</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">0.32</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">3.2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3.2</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2.2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2.2</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">0.22</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">0.22</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>&radic;8&radic;1.28 = &radic;(8 * 1.28) = &radic;10.24 = &radic;(1024/100) = &radic;((32 * 32)/(10 * 10)) = 32/10 = 3.2</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>How much money does Q have if P has Rs. 1265 which is 135 more than twice the money Q has? </p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; P &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360; &#2352;&#2369;. 1265 &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2332;&#2379; Q &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360; &#2350;&#2380;&#2332;&#2370;&#2342; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379;&#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; 135 &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; Q &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Rs. 700</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;. 700</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs. 430</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;. 430</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs. 630</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;. 630</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs. 565</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;. 565</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>P = 1265 = 135 + 2Q</p><p>1265 - 135 = 2Q</p><p>1130 = 2Q</p><p>565 = Q. </p><p>Hence, Q has <b>Rs. 565</b>. </p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which of the following pair of numbers is co-prime?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2366; &#2351;&#2369;&#2327;&#2381;&#2350; &#2309;&#2360;&#2361;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">(88, 81)</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">(88, 81)</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">(29, 87)</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">(29, 87)</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">(33, 39)</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">(33, 39)</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">(45, 48)</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">(45, 48)</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>HCF of 88 and 81 = 1</p><p>HCF of 29 and 87 = 29</p><p>HCF of 33 and 39 = 3</p><p>HCF of 45 and 48 = 3</p><p>Hence (88, 81) is co-prime.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The sum of two fractions is 1/2 and their difference is 3/14. Find the smallest fraction.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; 1/2 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; 3/14 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2366; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">1/7</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1/7</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1/14</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1/14</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2/9</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2/9</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4/21</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4/21</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Let smallest fraction = a</p><p>Then, largest fraction = a + 3/14</p><p>And, 1/2 = a + a + 3/14</p><p>4/14 = 2a</p><p><b>a = 1/7</b></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The square of one natural number is 39 greater than that of another natural number and their difference is 3. What is the value of 25% of their sum?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327;, &#2319;&#2325; &#2309;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2369;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 39 &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; 3 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2375; 25% &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">2.25</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2.25</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">3.25</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3.25</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2.75</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2.75</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">3.75</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3.75</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Let the larger and the smaller numbers be 'x' and 'y' respectively.</p><p>x<sup>2</sup>  -  y<sup>2</sup> = 39 and x  -  y = 3</p><p>So, x + y = (x<sup>2</sup>  -  y<sup>2</sup>)/(x  -  y) = 39/3 = 13</p><p>25% of (x + y) = 13/4 = 3.25</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The numerator of a fraction is increased by 140% and the denominator is decreased by 20%. The resulting fraction is 21/13. Find the original fraction.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2358; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 140% &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2361;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 20% &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2339;&#2366;&#2350;&#2368; &#2309;&#2306;&#2358; 21/13 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">9/13</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">9/13</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">8/13</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">8/13</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">11/13</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">11/13</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">7/13</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">7/13</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Let the original fraction be 'x/y'.</p><p>A/Q</p><p>x * 240/ y * 80 = 21/13</p><p>3x/y = 21/13</p><p>x/y = 7/13</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>What will be the reciprocal of the difference of the reciprocal of (5/11) and (6/5)?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>(5/11) &#2324;&#2352; (6/5) &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">30/41</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">30/41</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">25/41</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">25/41</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">41/30</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">41/30</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">41/25</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">41/25</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Difference of the reciprocal of (5/11) and (6/5) = (11/5)  -  (5/6)</p><p>= (66  -  25)/30</p><p>= 41/30</p><p>Reciprocal of difference = 30/41.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The sum of half of X, one-third of X, and third-fourth of X is less than 2 times of X by 40. Find the value of X.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>X &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2343;&#2375;, X &#2325;&#2375; 1/3 &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2324;&#2352; X &#2325;&#2375; 3/4 &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327;&#2347;&#2354;, X &#2325;&#2375; 2 &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2360;&#2375; 40 &#2325;&#2350; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; X &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">96</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">96</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">88</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">88</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">92</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">92</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">94</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">94</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>(X/2) + (X/3) + (3X/4) = 2X  -  40</p><p>(6X + 4X + 9X)/12 = 2X  -  40</p><p>19X = 24X  -  480</p><p>5X = 480</p><p>X = 96</p>","marks":2,"section":null}]}